The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Battery/**`. That path does
NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group — placing files there would not compile.
The repo's real, compiled canonical page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/`, where every
landed sibling P7 battery page ships (EnergyPage, BatteryCellsPage, BatteryDegradationPage,
SleepEfficiencyPage — ledger status=done) and which `Sources` already lists as a project.yml source
path (createIntermediateGroups: true). Page hosting uses the proven `*RouteRegistration` pattern
chained in `Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift`; tests live in `apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Battery/`.
The page therefore ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Battery/**` — the faithful equivalent of the
prompt's `Features/Battery`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This mapping is the only deviation
from the literal prompt path and is recorded here per covenant #9; it is identical to the
reconciliation used by every landed p4-apple P7 page.

The `/energy-products` web route had NO AppRoute case (`.energy` + `.powershare` are taken by sibling
surfaces), so a new `.energyProducts` case was added to AppRoute.swift (pathSegment `energy-products`,
group `.energy`, SF Symbol) — navigation registration, an allowed scope. `AppRouteParser` resolves
`/energy-products` → `.energyProducts` by pathSegment automatically (no alias needed); the host is
wired in TeslaSyncApp.swift right after the sibling EnergyRouteRegistration.

