SUMMARY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Native SwiftUI/HIG parity of the web EnergyProductsPage (route /energy-products), adaptive macOS + iOS
(ADR-002/006). Binds the @MainActor @Observable EnergyProductsPageModel through an injectable
EnergyProductsDataSource seam (ADR-004 — no networking in the view); the four web hooks are ported with
the same call-site names (loadSites/refreshSites/loadSiteInfo/refreshSiteInfo ← useTeslaEnergySites /
useRefreshTeslaEnergySites / useTeslaEnergySiteInfo / useRefreshTeslaEnergySiteInfo). Reproduces the web
chrome (title + subtitle + "Refresh from Tesla"), the four summary StatCards, and per-site cards
(header + battery-type badge, Charge/Capacity/Type stats, Solar/Battery/Grid/Backup/Storm-Watch +
Storm-Active capability badges, the site-configuration subsection — operation mode, the backup-reserve
RadialGauge, Powerwalls/Rated-Power/Rated-Energy StatCards, firmware + timezone, component badges, the
TOU rate-plan row + detail sheet, and the fetched stamp — plus the last-fetched footer). All from P2
tokens + P3 shared components (no hand-rolled glass, no direct Charts, no WKWebView). Every data source
implements loading/empty/error/success and every card its own site-info loading + empty states; the
nameplate StatCards always render (em-dash fallback, never a hidden panel). SI watt-hours/watts format
to kWh/kW at the render boundary exactly as the web page does. All 33 visible strings resolve from
Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names (39 keys added incl. 6 supplementary inline-label keys);
zero hardcoded literals. The web RadialGauge (a percentage) maps natively to the shared P3 TSRadialGauge.
